{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "tfcheck",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "AWS-CACHE-001",
              "name": "ElasticacheReplicationGroupDoesNotEncryptTrafficInTransit",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ElastiCache replication group does not encrypt traffic in transit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Without in-transit encryption, Redis traffic including AUTH tokens and cached data crosses the network in clear text."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without in-transit encryption, Redis traffic including AUTH tokens and cached data crosses the network in clear text.\n\nRemediation:\ntransit_encryption_enabled = true",
                "markdown": "Without in-transit encryption, Redis traffic including AUTH tokens and cached data crosses the network in clear text.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\ntransit_encryption_enabled = true\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-cache-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "encryption"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-CT-001",
              "name": "CloudtrailTrailIsNotMultiRegion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudTrail trail is not multi-region"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A single-region trail misses API activity in every other region, which is exactly where an attacker would spin up resources."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A single-region trail misses API activity in every other region, which is exactly where an attacker would spin up resources.\n\nRemediation:\nis_multi_region_trail = true",
                "markdown": "A single-region trail misses API activity in every other region, which is exactly where an attacker would spin up resources.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nis_multi_region_trail = true\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ct-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "logging"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-CT-002",
              "name": "CloudtrailLogFileValidationIsDisabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudTrail log file validation is disabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Log file validation produces signed digest files, so tampering with or deleting log files can be detected."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Log file validation produces signed digest files, so tampering with or deleting log files can be detected.\n\nRemediation:\nenable_log_file_validation = true",
                "markdown": "Log file validation produces signed digest files, so tampering with or deleting log files can be detected.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nenable_log_file_validation = true\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ct-002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "logging"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-CT-003",
              "name": "CloudtrailLogsAreNotEncryptedWithAKmsKey",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudTrail logs are not encrypted with a KMS key"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Encrypting trail logs with a customer managed KMS key adds a second access control: reading the logs also requires kms:Decrypt."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Encrypting trail logs with a customer managed KMS key adds a second access control: reading the logs also requires kms:Decrypt.\n\nRemediation:\nkms_key_id = aws_kms_key.cloudtrail.arn",
                "markdown": "Encrypting trail logs with a customer managed KMS key adds a second access control: reading the logs also requires kms:Decrypt.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nkms_key_id = aws_kms_key.cloudtrail.arn\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ct-003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "logging",
                  "encryption"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EC2-001",
              "name": "SecurityGroupAllowsIngressFromTheInternetToSensitivePorts",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Security group allows ingress from the internet to sensitive ports"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Remote administration (SSH, RDP, WinRM, VNC) and database or cache ports open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 are scanned constantly and brute-forced within minutes. Rules that open every port are reported as critical."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Remote administration (SSH, RDP, WinRM, VNC) and database or cache ports open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 are scanned constantly and brute-forced within minutes. Rules that open every port are reported as critical.\n\nRemediation:\nRestrict the source to known CIDR ranges or another security group, and reach instances through SSM Session Manager or a bastion instead of exposing admin ports.\n\ningress {\n  from_port   = 22\n  to_port     = 22\n  protocol    = \"tcp\"\n  cidr_blocks = [\"10.20.0.0/16\"]\n}",
                "markdown": "Remote administration (SSH, RDP, WinRM, VNC) and database or cache ports open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 are scanned constantly and brute-forced within minutes. Rules that open every port are reported as critical.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nRestrict the source to known CIDR ranges or another security group, and reach instances through SSM Session Manager or a bastion instead of exposing admin ports.\n\n```hcl\ningress {\n  from_port   = 22\n  to_port     = 22\n  protocol    = \"tcp\"\n  cidr_blocks = [\"10.20.0.0/16\"]\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ec2-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "network"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EC2-002",
              "name": "EbsStorageIsNotEncrypted",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EBS storage is not encrypted"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unencrypted EBS volumes and snapshots expose data to anyone who gains access to a snapshot copy or the underlying storage. Encryption is free and has no meaningful performance cost."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Unencrypted EBS volumes and snapshots expose data to anyone who gains access to a snapshot copy or the underlying storage. Encryption is free and has no meaningful performance cost.\n\nRemediation:\nSet encrypted = true on volumes and block device mappings, or turn on account-wide default encryption:\n\nresource \"aws_ebs_encryption_by_default\" \"this\" {\n  enabled = true\n}",
                "markdown": "Unencrypted EBS volumes and snapshots expose data to anyone who gains access to a snapshot copy or the underlying storage. Encryption is free and has no meaningful performance cost.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nSet encrypted = true on volumes and block device mappings, or turn on account-wide default encryption:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aws_ebs_encryption_by_default\" \"this\" {\n  enabled = true\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ec2-002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "encryption"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EC2-003",
              "name": "InstanceMetadataServiceAllowsImdsv1",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Instance metadata service allows IMDSv1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IMDSv1 answers unauthenticated GET requests, so any SSRF bug in an application on the instance can be used to steal its IAM role credentials. IMDSv2 requires a session token and blocks this."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "IMDSv1 answers unauthenticated GET requests, so any SSRF bug in an application on the instance can be used to steal its IAM role credentials. IMDSv2 requires a session token and blocks this.\n\nRemediation:\nmetadata_options {\n  http_endpoint = \"enabled\"\n  http_tokens   = \"required\"\n}",
                "markdown": "IMDSv1 answers unauthenticated GET requests, so any SSRF bug in an application on the instance can be used to steal its IAM role credentials. IMDSv2 requires a session token and blocks this.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nmetadata_options {\n  http_endpoint = \"enabled\"\n  http_tokens   = \"required\"\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ec2-003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "credentials"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EC2-004",
              "name": "InstanceGetsAPublicIpAddress",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Instance gets a public IP address"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Instances with public IPs are directly reachable from the internet, so a single security group mistake exposes them. Put workloads in private subnets behind a load balancer or NAT."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Instances with public IPs are directly reachable from the internet, so a single security group mistake exposes them. Put workloads in private subnets behind a load balancer or NAT.\n\nRemediation:\nRemove associate_public_ip_address (or set it to false) and place the instance in a private subnet.",
                "markdown": "Instances with public IPs are directly reachable from the internet, so a single security group mistake exposes them. Put workloads in private subnets behind a load balancer or NAT.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nRemove associate_public_ip_address (or set it to false) and place the instance in a private subnet."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ec2-004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "network"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EC2-005",
              "name": "DefaultSecurityGroupAllowsTraffic",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Default security group allows traffic"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Resources launched without an explicit security group land in the VPC default group. It should allow nothing, so that mistake fails closed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Resources launched without an explicit security group land in the VPC default group. It should allow nothing, so that mistake fails closed.\n\nRemediation:\nManage the default group with no ingress or egress blocks:\n\nresource \"aws_default_security_group\" \"default\" {\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n}",
                "markdown": "Resources launched without an explicit security group land in the VPC default group. It should allow nothing, so that mistake fails closed.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nManage the default group with no ingress or egress blocks:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aws_default_security_group\" \"default\" {\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ec2-005",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "network"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-ECR-001",
              "name": "EcrRepositoryDoesNotScanImagesOnPush",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ECR repository does not scan images on push"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Scanning on push catches known-vulnerable packages before images are deployed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Scanning on push catches known-vulnerable packages before images are deployed.\n\nRemediation:\nimage_scanning_configuration {\n  scan_on_push = true\n}",
                "markdown": "Scanning on push catches known-vulnerable packages before images are deployed.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nimage_scanning_configuration {\n  scan_on_push = true\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-ecr-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "supply-chain"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EFS-001",
              "name": "EfsFileSystemIsNotEncrypted",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EFS file system is not encrypted"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "EFS encryption at rest can only be chosen at creation time."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "EFS encryption at rest can only be chosen at creation time.\n\nRemediation:\nencrypted = true",
                "markdown": "EFS encryption at rest can only be chosen at creation time.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nencrypted = true\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-efs-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "encryption"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-EKS-001",
              "name": "EksApiEndpointIsOpenToTheInternet",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EKS API endpoint is open to the internet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "By default the Kubernetes API server endpoint is public and accepts connections from 0.0.0.0/0. Any leaked kubeconfig or API vulnerability is then exploitable from anywhere."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "By default the Kubernetes API server endpoint is public and accepts connections from 0.0.0.0/0. Any leaked kubeconfig or API vulnerability is then exploitable from anywhere.\n\nRemediation:\nvpc_config {\n  endpoint_private_access = true\n  endpoint_public_access  = false  # or restrict public_access_cidrs\n}",
                "markdown": "By default the Kubernetes API server endpoint is public and accepts connections from 0.0.0.0/0. Any leaked kubeconfig or API vulnerability is then exploitable from anywhere.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nvpc_config {\n  endpoint_private_access = true\n  endpoint_public_access  = false  # or restrict public_access_cidrs\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-eks-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "network"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-ELB-001",
              "name": "LoadBalancerListenerServesPlainHttp",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer listener serves plain HTTP"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An HTTP listener that forwards traffic (instead of redirecting to HTTPS) sends credentials and session cookies in clear text."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An HTTP listener that forwards traffic (instead of redirecting to HTTPS) sends credentials and session cookies in clear text.\n\nRemediation:\ndefault_action {\n  type = \"redirect\"\n  redirect {\n    port        = \"443\"\n    protocol    = \"HTTPS\"\n    status_code = \"HTTP_301\"\n  }\n}",
                "markdown": "An HTTP listener that forwards traffic (instead of redirecting to HTTPS) sends credentials and session cookies in clear text.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\ndefault_action {\n  type = \"redirect\"\n  redirect {\n    port        = \"443\"\n    protocol    = \"HTTPS\"\n    status_code = \"HTTP_301\"\n  }\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-elb-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "encryption",
                  "network"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-ELB-002",
              "name": "LoadBalancerListenerAllowsTlsOr",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer listener allows TLS 1.0 or 1.1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are deprecated (RFC 8996). Older ELB security policies, including the historical default ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08, still negotiate them."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are deprecated (RFC 8996). Older ELB security policies, including the historical default ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08, still negotiate them.\n\nRemediation:\nssl_policy = \"ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06\"",
                "markdown": "TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are deprecated (RFC 8996). Older ELB security policies, including the historical default ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08, still negotiate them.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nssl_policy = \"ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06\"\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-elb-002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "encryption"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-IAM-001",
              "name": "IamPolicyGrantsFullAdministratorAccess",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM policy grants full administrator access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A statement allowing Action \"*\" on Resource \"*\" is full admin. Anyone or anything that can use this policy can disable logging, create users and take over the account."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A statement allowing Action \"*\" on Resource \"*\" is full admin. Anyone or anything that can use this policy can disable logging, create users and take over the account.\n\nRemediation:\nGrant only the actions and resources the workload needs. IAM Access Analyzer can generate a least-privilege policy from CloudTrail activity.",
                "markdown": "A statement allowing Action \"*\" on Resource \"*\" is full admin. Anyone or anything that can use this policy can disable logging, create users and take over the account.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nGrant only the actions and resources the workload needs. IAM Access Analyzer can generate a least-privilege policy from CloudTrail activity."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-iam-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "iam",
                  "least-privilege"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-IAM-002",
              "name": "IamPolicyUsesServiceWideWildcardActions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM policy uses service-wide wildcard actions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Actions such as \"s3:*\" or \"iam:*\", or an Allow with NotAction, grant every current and future permission of a service, including destructive and privilege-escalation actions."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Actions such as \"s3:*\" or \"iam:*\", or an Allow with NotAction, grant every current and future permission of a service, including destructive and privilege-escalation actions.\n\nRemediation:\nList the specific actions needed, for example [\"s3:GetObject\", \"s3:PutObject\"] instead of \"s3:*\".",
                "markdown": "Actions such as \"s3:*\" or \"iam:*\", or an Allow with NotAction, grant every current and future permission of a service, including destructive and privilege-escalation actions.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nList the specific actions needed, for example [\"s3:GetObject\", \"s3:PutObject\"] instead of \"s3:*\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-iam-002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "iam",
                  "least-privilege"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-IAM-003",
              "name": "AdministratoraccessManagedPolicyIsAttached",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AdministratorAccess managed policy is attached"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The AWS managed AdministratorAccess policy grants every action on every resource. Attaching it to roles used by workloads or CI turns any compromise of that workload into a full account takeover."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The AWS managed AdministratorAccess policy grants every action on every resource. Attaching it to roles used by workloads or CI turns any compromise of that workload into a full account takeover.\n\nRemediation:\nAttach a scoped customer managed policy instead, and reserve administrator access for break-glass roles protected by MFA.",
                "markdown": "The AWS managed AdministratorAccess policy grants every action on every resource. Attaching it to roles used by workloads or CI turns any compromise of that workload into a full account takeover.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nAttach a scoped customer managed policy instead, and reserve administrator access for break-glass roles protected by MFA."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-iam-003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "iam",
                  "least-privilege"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-IAM-004",
              "name": "IamRoleCanBeAssumedByAnyPrincipal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM role can be assumed by any principal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A trust policy that allows Principal \"*\" (or AWS \"*\") to call sts:AssumeRole without a condition lets any AWS account in the world assume the role."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A trust policy that allows Principal \"*\" (or AWS \"*\") to call sts:AssumeRole without a condition lets any AWS account in the world assume the role.\n\nRemediation:\nTrust specific accounts, roles or services, and require sts:ExternalId or aws:PrincipalOrgID conditions for cross-account access.",
                "markdown": "A trust policy that allows Principal \"*\" (or AWS \"*\") to call sts:AssumeRole without a condition lets any AWS account in the world assume the role.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nTrust specific accounts, roles or services, and require sts:ExternalId or aws:PrincipalOrgID conditions for cross-account access."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-iam-004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "iam"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-IAM-005",
              "name": "IamPolicyIsAttachedDirectlyToAUser",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM policy is attached directly to a user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Permissions granted to individual users are hard to audit and tend to outlive the person's role. Grant permissions to groups or roles."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Permissions granted to individual users are hard to audit and tend to outlive the person's role. Grant permissions to groups or roles.\n\nRemediation:\nAttach the policy to an aws_iam_group and add the user to the group, or move humans to IAM Identity Center.",
                "markdown": "Permissions granted to individual users are hard to audit and tend to outlive the person's role. Grant permissions to groups or roles.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nAttach the policy to an aws_iam_group and add the user to the group, or move humans to IAM Identity Center."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-iam-005",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "iam"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-KMS-001",
              "name": "KmsKeyRotationIsDisabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "KMS key rotation is disabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Automatic rotation limits how much data is protected by any one key version. It only applies to symmetric encryption keys."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Automatic rotation limits how much data is protected by any one key version. It only applies to symmetric encryption keys.\n\nRemediation:\nenable_key_rotation = true",
                "markdown": "Automatic rotation limits how much data is protected by any one key version. It only applies to symmetric encryption keys.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nenable_key_rotation = true\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-kms-001",
