            {
              "id": "AWS-S3-001",
              "name": "S3BucketAclGrantsPublicAccess",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket ACL grants public access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A canned ACL of public-read, public-read-write or authenticated-read lets anyone on the internet (or any AWS account) list or modify objects. Public ACLs are the classic cause of S3 data leaks."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A canned ACL of public-read, public-read-write or authenticated-read lets anyone on the internet (or any AWS account) list or modify objects. Public ACLs are the classic cause of S3 data leaks.\n\nRemediation:\nUse a private ACL (or disable ACLs entirely with object ownership \"BucketOwnerEnforced\") and serve public content through CloudFront with origin access control instead.\n\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  rule { object_ownership = \"BucketOwnerEnforced\" }\n}",
                "markdown": "A canned ACL of public-read, public-read-write or authenticated-read lets anyone on the internet (or any AWS account) list or modify objects. Public ACLs are the classic cause of S3 data leaks.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nUse a private ACL (or disable ACLs entirely with object ownership \"BucketOwnerEnforced\") and serve public content through CloudFront with origin access control instead.\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  rule { object_ownership = \"BucketOwnerEnforced\" }\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-s3-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "data-exposure"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-S3-002",
              "name": "S3BucketIsNotCoveredByAFullPublicAccessBlock",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket is not covered by a full public access block"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "S3 Block Public Access is the guard rail that stops a future ACL or bucket policy change from exposing data. Every bucket should have all four settings enabled, either on the bucket or account-wide."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "S3 Block Public Access is the guard rail that stops a future ACL or bucket policy change from exposing data. Every bucket should have all four settings enabled, either on the bucket or account-wide.\n\nRemediation:\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"this\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}",
                "markdown": "S3 Block Public Access is the guard rail that stops a future ACL or bucket policy change from exposing data. Every bucket should have all four settings enabled, either on the bucket or account-wide.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"this\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-s3-002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "data-exposure"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-S3-003",
              "name": "S3BucketPolicyAllowsAccessFromAnyPrincipal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket policy allows access from any principal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A bucket policy statement with Effect Allow and Principal \"*\" and no Condition grants that access to everyone on the internet."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A bucket policy statement with Effect Allow and Principal \"*\" and no Condition grants that access to everyone on the internet.\n\nRemediation:\nName the specific AWS principals that need access, or add a Condition (for example aws:SourceVpce, aws:PrincipalOrgID or aws:SourceArn) that narrows who can use the statement.",
                "markdown": "A bucket policy statement with Effect Allow and Principal \"*\" and no Condition grants that access to everyone on the internet.\n\n**Remediation**\n\nName the specific AWS principals that need access, or add a Condition (for example aws:SourceVpce, aws:PrincipalOrgID or aws:SourceArn) that narrows who can use the statement."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-s3-003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "data-exposure"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-S3-004",
              "name": "S3BucketVersioningIsNotEnabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket versioning is not enabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Without versioning, an overwritten or deleted object is gone for good, which turns ransomware or a bad deploy script into permanent data loss."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without versioning, an overwritten or deleted object is gone for good, which turns ransomware or a bad deploy script into permanent data loss.\n\nRemediation:\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  versioning_configuration { status = \"Enabled\" }\n}",
                "markdown": "Without versioning, an overwritten or deleted object is gone for good, which turns ransomware or a bad deploy script into permanent data loss.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  versioning_configuration { status = \"Enabled\" }\n}\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-s3-004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "terraform",
                  "aws",
                  "resilience"
                ],
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AWS-SNS-001",
              "name": "SnsTopicIsNotEncrypted",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "SNS topic is not encrypted"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Messages in an unencrypted topic are stored in plain text. Use a KMS key so access to message content is also controlled by key policy."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Messages in an unencrypted topic are stored in plain text. Use a KMS key so access to message content is also controlled by key policy.\n\nRemediation:\nkms_master_key_id = \"alias/aws/sns\"  # or a customer managed key",
                "markdown": "Messages in an unencrypted topic are stored in plain text. Use a KMS key so access to message content is also controlled by key policy.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n```hcl\nkms_master_key_id = \"alias/aws/sns\"  # or a customer managed key\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/DaveyD347/terraform-misconfig-checker/blob/main/docs/rules.md#aws-sns-001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
